    "ranking_validity": {
      "mechanism": "Ranking by distance to TARGET flatters any target near the start area regardless of where its object begins.",
      "note": "The metric is not uniformly wrong - it is EXACTLY right on the luckiest permutation and ANTI-CORRELATED on the unluckiest, and S4 9.6 decides which after quarantine. note_white ranks first on the model and last at the worst draw: its target is the closest to the start area while its note can begin 1760 mm away.",
      "spearman_at_best_permutation": 1.0,
      "spearman_at_worst_permutation": -0.486
    },
    "what": "distance_from_start_mm and round_trip_mm measure start_area to target and omit the leg that fetches the object. The claim in scope.answers, 'what each mission costs in travel', is therefore not supported.",
    "why_it_matters": "The error runs both ways, so points_per_metre_round_trip does not preserve the ranking it appears to give."
  },
